//
//  The catalogue, compiled in. JSON so it reads as data and can be printed,
//  checked and diffed; a Swift string so it ships inside the binary (a
//  Homebrew-symlinked tool cannot find a resource bundle).
//
//  EVERY ENTRY WAS PROBED on the Mac named in "probed": read, and for each
//  writable one, a scratch value written through CFPreferences, read back by
//  a separate process (`defaults read`), and the original put back and
//  confirmed — type and all. "verified" lists the macOS major versions that
//  was done on. An entry nobody probed does not belong here.
//
//  "restart" is what the setting is documented to need; the probe measured
//  that the value is stored and seen by other processes, not that the Dock
//  redrew. "default" is what the key means when unset; null when not known.
//

